Here’s a **compact, native UE5.8 C++ design** for driving a render-only skeletal mesh (e.g., Epic Offroad chassis) from your existing non-authoritative vehicle simulation, using **PoseableMeshComponent** as the preferred lightweight solution (no AnimBlueprint overhead), with optional `AnimInstanceProxy` extension path.

---

### **Design Tradeoffs: PoseableMesh vs. AnimInstanceProxy**

| Criterion | **PoseableMeshComponent** (Recommended) | **AnimInstanceProxy (Full BP/AnimGraph)** |
|---------|----------------------------------------|------------------------------------------|
| **CPU Overhead** | Very low (direct transform updates) | Higher (IK passes, notifies, state machines) |
| **Network Support** | Not replicated (intended cosmetic) | Same (if not marked `SimulatedProxy`), but more moving parts to sync |
| **Simplicity** | ✅ Pure C++ pose update (no animation assets needed) | Requires animation blueprint, retargeting, root motion handling |
| **Deform Skin Support** | ❌ Bone transforms only (no procedural muscle deform) | ✅ Can drive morph targets, cloth via curves if needed later |
| **Maintenance** | ✅ Single function to update transforms | More code/config boundary (BP + C++) |
| **TempoSafety** | ✅ Safe in `TickComponent` when owner is `SimulatedProxy` | Risk of late-authoritative override if not `PrePhysics` |

→ **Verdict**: For *render-only*, *non-authoritative*, *wheel-driven* chassis, **PoseableMeshComponent** is optimal. Reserve `AnimInstanceProxy` only if future deformation/morphing is required.

---

### **Core Implementation Sketch (PoseableMeshComponent)**

```cpp
// .h
UCLASS(BlueprintType, meta=(BlueprintSpawnableComponent))
class YOURGAME_API UOffroadChassisProxy : public UPoseableMeshComponent
{
    GENERATED_BODY()

public:
    UOffroadChassisProxy();

    // Expects 4 wheel positions/steering/rotation in local space
    UFUNCTION(BlueprintCallable, Category = "Chassis")
    void UpdateFromWheelData(
        const FVector& FLWheel, const FVector& FRWheel,
        const FVector& RLWheel, const FVector& RRWheel,
        float FLSteer, float FRSteer,    // rad, absolute (left+ = steer right for offroad convention)
        float WheelSpinAngleFL, 
        float WheelSpinAngleFR,
        float WheelSpinAngleRL,
        float WheelSpinAngleRR
    );

    // Cache for interpolation (optional)
    UPARAM(EditAnywhere) float bDebugShowProxies = false;

private:
    // Bone names from skeletal mesh (matching your asset)
    FName RootBoneName = TEXT("pelvis"); // Typical UE4/5 offroad skeleton root
    FName FLWheelBone = TEXT("Wheel_Front_Left");
    FName FRWheelBone = TEXT("Wheel_Front_Right");
    FName RLWheelBone = TEXT("Wheel_Rear_Left");
    FName RRWheelBone = TEXT("Wheel_Rear_Right");
    FName SteeringFLBone = TEXT("Steering_Left");
    FName SteeringFRBone = TEXT("Steering_Right");
};
